     The Internet is a large and complex aggregation of network hardware, con‐
     nected together by gateways.  Tracking the route packets follow (or find‐
     ing the miscreant gateway that's discarding packets) can be difficult.
     ttrraacceerroouuttee and ttrraacceerroouuttee66 attempt to elicit TIME_EXCEEDED responses from
     each gateway along the path to _h_o_s_t, in order to determine their route.
     ttrraacceerroouuttee is used for IPv4 networks and ttrraacceerroouuttee66 for IPv6.

